{
    "background_story": "Jade was a devout Catholic who took her faith very seriously. Every year, she would observe the Lenten season with great fervor, using the 40-day period to reflect on her life and spiritual growth. She would give up something she loved, like her favorite coffee, and instead focus on prayer, charity, and self-improvement. One Lenten season, Jade decided to volunteer at a local soup kitchen, where she met many people struggling to make ends meet. Her experience was life-changing, and she realized that true sacrifice wasn't just about giving up something, but about giving to others. From then on, Jade continued to serve at the soup kitchen, even after Lent was over, and inspired others to do the same. Her Lenten journey had taught her the value of selflessness and compassion.",
